{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Your sun, etc.</b> This is the sun, which will not set, and the moon, which will not be gathered, for the meaning is that when it is conjoined with the sun, then light will be absent from the earth." "<b>And your days of mourning shall be completed.</b> For mourning dwells in darkness."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:30.225995511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}